Subject: [PATCH] gnome-desktop: use the installed iso-codes prefix

The cross pkg-config wrapper correctly points compilers into the sysroot, but
that makes dependency.get_variable('prefix') a build-machine path. Embedding it
in libgnome-desktop makes language and country data unavailable at runtime.
iso-codes is installed beside gnome-desktop, so use the target Meson prefix.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ endif
 
 fontconfig_cache_path = fontconfig_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'cachedir')
 xkb_base = xkb_config_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'xkb_base')
-iso_codes_prefix = iso_codes_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'prefix')
+iso_codes_prefix = get_option('prefix')
 
 cc = meson.get_compiler('c')
 
